- If the provided buffer size is sufficient, it appends a `/` to the end of the modified filename and stores the result in the output buffer. Otherwise, it uses a local temporary buffer to perform the operation and then copies the result into the provided buffer.
- The function supports Unicode characters correctly using wide character functions (wcslen, wcscpy, etc.) and handles internationalized strings efficiently.
